--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/design/pi-footer-startup.md
@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Pi footer at startup: no swap, no gap, same in every directory
+
+Parity reference: Pi 1.4.0. Fixture: the maintainer's Pi setup (13 autoloaded packages,
+`ghostty-dark`, `tuiMode: fullscreen`), model `gpt-5.6-luna` named `GPT-5.6 Luna`, 272K context.
+
+## What owns the footer
+
+Pi's built-in footer (`0.0%/272k (auto)` and the model on one line) is replaced by the
+`powerline-footer` extension of `pi-agent-extensions` 0.5.4: `ctx.ui.setFooter(...)` in
+`session_start`. Its single row is `<short cwd> ... <model name> <used>/<window> (<pct>%)
+[| $cost (sub)] | <elapsed> <clock>`, followed by ` | <extension statuses>`, and the whole row is
+cut to the terminal width with `...`. That is why the maintainer's Pi shows `1m 22...` at the end.
+No other autoloaded package sets a footer (`pi-zentui`, which does, is `autoload: false`).
+
+## Findings (octet before this change, warm, 120 columns)
+
+| t | footer rows |
+|---|---|
+| 0.0 s | none |
+| 0.04 s | octet's own footer `GPT-5.6 Luna · 1%/272K · $0   <path>` |
+| 13.6 s | still octet's footer, `PI-EVAL-READY` printed under it |
+| 14.2 s | blank footer row (the mount exists, its first frame has not arrived) |
+| 14.5 s | the Pi footer |
+
+1. **Swap.** The extension mounts seconds after the first frame; until then the host draws its
+   own footer, then a blank row, then the live one.
+2. **Cwd = home never loads the Pi setup.** `discoverPiSetup` treats everything under
+   `<cwd>/.pi` as project scope. From the home directory that contains the user's agent dir
+   (`~/.pi/agent`), so with an untrusted workspace every extension, theme and keybinding was
+   dropped as "untrusted project .pi paths are not mirrored" and `factories=0`: the footer
+   never appears and octet's footer stays. `lib/pi-setup.mjs` now excludes the agent dir from
+   the project-trust gate (user scope, as in Pi).
+3. **Fidelity.** With the fixture model the live footer is already cell for cell Pi's: same
+   cells, same colours. The facts it reads (`ctx.model.name`, `getContextUsage()`,
+   `modelRegistry.isUsingOAuth`) come from the host's model view, which carries name, window and
+   `oauth`.
+
+## Design: placeholder per workspace, drawn by a generic host primitive
+
+The host (Pi-agnostic) keeps the plain text of the first live extension footer per workspace in
+`~/.octet/cache/footer/<hash>.json` (`tui/footer_placeholder.rs`): columns, the sorted names of
+the extensions that were starting, and at most 8 rows of 4 KiB. At the next launch it:
+
+- loads it when the shell is entered and draws it dimmed in the footer's position, including
+  the startup composer's reserved footer row, so octet's footer never paints;
+- keeps it only when the extensions starting at `frame.ready` are exactly the recorded ones;
+- keeps its height at any other width (blank rows) rather than drawing misaligned text;
+- keeps it while the footer is mounted but has not painted (this was the blank row);
+- drops it when the live footer paints (the live rows take the same position, so nothing moves)
+  or when extension startup settles without a footer (octet's footer returns).
+
